# Production build (required)

This project ships as a single minified `production.html` for mobile.

## After every source change

Whenever you edit **any** of these, run the production build before finishing:

- `main.html`, `main.js`
- `shared/css/_variables.css` (brand theme tokens mapped onto Bootstrap)
- Any file under `shared/lib/`
- Any file under `shared/db/`
- Any file under `features/`
- `shared/scripts/manifest.json`
- `app-version.json` (version + build stamp for More page)
- `build-production.js`

```bash
npm run build
```

`npm run build` always **bumps the patch version** and stamps date/time on the More page (`app-version.json`). Use `npm run build:nobump` only for quiet rebuilds (e.g. editor hooks).

`npm run save` bumps + builds **before** commit/push so the pushed build always carries a new version.

Do this **voluntarily at the end of your turn** even if the user did not ask. Do not skip because hooks may also run — always confirm with `npm run build` after your edits.

## Rules

- Never edit `production.html` by hand.
- Bootstrap CSS/JS load from CDN (not bundled into production.html).
- Brand colors live only in `shared/css/_variables.css` (inlined into production.html).
- If the build fails, fix the error and run `npm run build` again.
- Report the built file size when you changed source files.
